  "details": "- CVE-2017-7486, CVE-2017-7547: restrict pg_user_mappings view to hide user mapping passwords from unauthorized users\n- CVE-2017-12172: do not open the startup log as root in the init script, and create it as postgres\n- CVE-2019-10208: prevent type lookups from executing code in a user-controlled search_path\n- CVE-2020-25694: keep connection security parameters when pg_restore or psql \\connect reconnects\n- CVE-2020-25695: block enqueue of at-commit user code in security-restricted operations\n- CVE-2021-23214: reject extraneous data after an SSL request in the startup packet\n- CVE-2021-32027: fix buffer overruns with invalid array subscripts",
